# Build artifacts. Regenerable from tools/ + resources/, never a source of
# truth. The published copies live in docs/packs/ and the frozen regression
# baselines in tests/fixtures/ -- both of those ARE tracked.
# Every .txt in tools/ is a build artifact: the builders write
# <slug>-all-specs.txt and <slug>-<spec>.txt there, and mksite.py republishes
# them to docs/packs/. This was `tools/runemaster-*.txt` and therefore missed
# Chronomancer entirely -- a per-class line is one more thing to remember for
# each of the 21 classes, so match the directory instead. Nothing tracked in
# tools/ has ever been a .txt.
#
# The packs now live one folder down, in tools/packs/<slug>/ (with the
# diagnostic strings under tools/packs/_diag/). `tools/*.txt` does NOT match a
# nested path, so the directory needs its own line -- keep both: the flat one
# still catches anything written beside the scripts.
tools/*.txt
tools/packs/
tools/guide.html
output/

# Scraped snapshots under resources/ are deliberately NOT ignored: they are
# third-party pages that can change or vanish, which makes them the least
# reproducible asset here. resources/in-game-verified.json is ground truth read
# off tooltips and cannot be regenerated at all. See NOTICE.

# audit_cds.py's per-spell scrape cache: 338 raw Firecrawl response envelopes,
# ~1.5M, keyed by spell id. Ignored rather than kept, because unlike the
# resources/ snapshots these are not the asset -- the facts distilled out of
# them (cd, gcd, specs) land in resources/cooldown-abilities.json, which IS
# tracked. Delete the directory to force a full re-scrape.
tools/spellchk/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.gstack/
.claude/worktrees/
